From: Salt OpenWrt packaging
Subject: [PATCH] loader: discover adjacent sourceless Python bytecode

OpenWrt uses compileall -b and removes Python sources. LazyLoader already
has a SourcelessFileLoader and supports __init__.pyc packages, but skips
adjacent module.pyc during discovery. Allow these through the existing
suffix/optimization ordering, which continues to prefer .py over .pyc.
Importlib still validates the bytecode header when loading.

--- a/salt/loader/lazy.py
+++ b/salt/loader/lazy.py
@@ -730,12 +730,6 @@
                             # exists, so skip this.
                             continue
 
-                    if not dirname and ext == ".pyc":
-                        # On Python 3, we should only load .pyc files from the
-                        # __pycache__ subdirectory (i.e. when dirname is not an
-                        # empty string).
-                        continue
-
                     # Made it this far - add it
                     self.file_mapping[f_noext] = (fpath, ext, opt_index)
 
